<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Agen</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Aginnum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Agen is a city in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garonne">Garonne</a>, capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lot-et-garonne">Lot-et-Garonne</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a>. As Aginnum it was the chief town of the Gallic Nitiobroges, and in 107 BCE the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigurini">Tigurini</a> defeated a Roman army in its region. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was a bishopric and the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agenais">Agenais</a>, which passed between the English and French crowns.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/agen.jpg" alt="Agen" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: KoS · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vue_Agen_3.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
